### =====================================================================
### ShopEasy - the full API flow for the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Start the app first (mvn spring-boot:run), then click "Send Request" above each request,
### TOP TO BOTTOM. Named requests (# @name) let later requests reuse tokens and ids.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@json = application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. AUTH
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1a. Register a new customer (change the email if you run it twice -> otherwise 409)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "fullName": "Asha Verma",
  "email": "asha@example.com",
  "password": "Secret@123"
}

### 1b. Log in as the seeded customer
# @name customerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "email": "customer@shopeasy.com",
  "password": "Customer@123"
}

### 1c. Log in as the seeded admin
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "email": "admin@shopeasy.com",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

### Tokens taken from the responses above
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1d. Who am I?
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 1e. Wrong password -> 401 ProblemDetail
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "email": "customer@shopeasy.com", "password": "wrong" }

### 1f. Invalid registration -> 400 with field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "fullName": "", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "short" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. BROWSE (public - no token)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2a. All categories (cached)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories

### 2b. Products: first page, 5 per page, most expensive first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?page=0&size=5&sort=price,desc

### 2c. Search: text + category + price range + only in stock
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=book&categoryId=2&minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&inStock=true

### 2d. One product (second call is served from the cache - watch the log)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/2

### 2e. Unknown product -> 404 ProblemDetail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/9999

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. CART (CUSTOMER)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3a. Add 2 x Wireless Earbuds Pro (id 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "productId": 2, "quantity": 2 }

### 3b. Add 1 x Java for Beginners (id 5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "productId": 5, "quantity": 1 }

### 3c. Change the quantity of product 5 to 3
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items/5
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "quantity": 3 }

### 3d. Show my cart
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 3e. Too many: Smart Watch Fit (id 4) has only 3 in stock -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "productId": 4, "quantity": 10 }

### 3f. Cart without a token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cart

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. ORDERS (CUSTOMER)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4a. Place an order from the cart -> 201 + Location header
# @name placeOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "shippingAddress": "12 MG Road, Bengaluru 560001" }

@orderId = {{placeOrder.response.body.id}}

### 4b. Check that the stock of product 2 went down by 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/2

### 4c. My orders (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 4d. One order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 4e. Placing an order with an empty cart -> 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "shippingAddress": "Anywhere" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. ADMIN
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5a. Create a category
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "name": "Sports", "description": "Sports and fitness equipment" }

### 5b. Create a product
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "sku": "SPORT-001",
  "name": "Yoga Mat",
  "description": "6 mm thick, non-slip",
  "price": 1499.00,
  "stockQuantity": 25,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 5c. Update a product (PUT = full replacement; the SKU must stay the same)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/12
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "sku": "FASH-002",
  "name": "Cotton T-Shirt",
  "description": "100% organic cotton, regular fit",
  "price": 449.00,
  "stockQuantity": 450,
  "categoryId": 4
}

### 5d. Soft-delete a product
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5e. All orders (filter by status is optional)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders?status=PENDING
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5f. Move the order forward: PENDING -> PAID -> SHIPPED -> DELIVERED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "status": "PAID" }

### 5g. A customer trying an admin endpoint -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "name": "Hacked" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. CANCEL + OPERATIONS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6a. Customer cancels the order (allowed while PENDING or PAID) - stock is returned
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 6b. Health (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### 6c. Info (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/info

### 6d. Caches (ADMIN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/caches
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6e. Metrics: number of HTTP requests (ADMIN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics/http.server.requests
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
